  The first-start journey's account sheets, read from the live file on
  2026-10-13 with `get_metadata`, with the component instances expanded.

  `70-28.xml` carries these frames from the page export, but every `Choice /`
  and `Action /` in them is a stub — the same blind spot that made a dedicated
  capture necessary for the sign-in screen (`176-10686.xml`). This file is the
  expansion, for the two sheets that stand between a fresh machine and a
  person who can use it.

  Reference size 1440 x 960. Every number is a logical pixel.

  Read with `get_metadata`, so: ids, names, x, y, width, height and `hidden`.
  **Effects and strokes are not in it** - a stroke on a frame is not a child
  layer, which `MANIFEST.md` records as the blind spot that hid the window
  edge's focus ring and the sign-in entry's error border. Colours and type
  must be read from a render or from `variables.toml`, never assumed.

  ## The sheets share one skeleton

  Both frames below are the same composition with different contents, and
  `ROOTS.md` says the rule is structural rather than a list: *a frame carries
  the strip when it is a setup sheet*. So this is one layout to build once and
  fill many times, the way `crate::sign_in_layout` is one layout for the
  sign-in and unlock screens.

      Wallpaper / folded light   0,0      1440 x 960
      Stage                      950,52    420 x 18
      Main / <name>              160,164   600 x <tall>
        Eyebrow                    0,0     600 x 16
        Title                      0,32    600 x <tall>
        Introduction               0,<y>   600 x <tall>
        Choices                    0,<y>   600 x 180
          <a choice>               0,0     600 x 85
          <a choice>               0,95    600 x 85
        Consequence                0,<y>   600 x 22
        Actions                    0,<y>   600 x 48
          <an action>              0,0     160 x 48
          <an action>            172,0     160 x 48   (176 wide where the words need it)
      Action / Accessibility      40,876   160 x 48
      Footer                     736,892   640 x 16

  **The column is left-aligned at x=160**, not centred: a setup sheet is read,
  and the sign-in screen's centred group is for a screen that is answered.

  ## The wallpaper is the one already drawn

  `371:30183` and `371:30390` below carry the same five vectors, at the same
  coordinates, as `364:25552` in `176-10686.xml` — the artwork
  `crate::sign_in_wallpaper` already rasterises. One wallpaper for the whole
  first start and the sign-in screen alike; nothing new to transcribe.

  ## Still owed by this capture

  - The `Choice /` component's own states. Each is 600 x 85 with a Title at
    (21, 17) and a Description at (21, 46); whether it draws a field, a
    border, or a selected state is **not** in the metadata and must be read
    from a render before anything is drawn.
  - Every `Action /` instance is a stub here: 160 x 48 and nothing about what
    is inside it.
  - The nine other frames of the journey — Welcome, language, region,
    keyboard, Protect your computer, Sign-in options, fingerprint, recovery
    and the AI choice — are listed in `ROOTS.md` and not captured here.
-->
